WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Install QA FlowKit from your project terminal and select your agent adapter. This is the only terminal step in the walkthrough.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Now open the same repository in your model's CLI. Enter slash qa init. The agent asks about languages, templates, sources and tools. Review its proposal before approving changes.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:42.000
If you have a local folder of team QA practices, you can start with this alternative, still inside the model. The agent summarizes context and asks approval for inferred decisions.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Stay inside the model's CLI. Use slash qa doctor to check setup. Then slash qa help recommends the next step based on your repository's current state.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:16.000
To follow the workflow, use slash qa full flow with your requirements file. You can also supply the text when the agent asks. Confirm the official identifier RF one hundred and one. The agent presents a plan and guides you through the phases.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Review the test design and respond to approval requests inside the conversation. You do not need to run internal scripts manually or advance phases from another terminal.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:42.000
To check Gherkin, use slash qa validate features. Ask the agent to explain and correct any issues. Validating these files does not mean the login tests ran.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Use slash qa status to review outcomes and pending work. Slash qa help recommends how to continue. To add tests for another requirement, use slash qa add tests.
